GtkACE 0.6.0 (2026-11-07)

  More command dialogs (Commands menu, and the map's right-click menu):
  - Attack: lists your sectors next to the target with their military,
    and the land units there.  Choose how many to send from each
    sector and which units go; GtkACE answers the server's questions
    from your choices (including moving in after a win).
  - Fire: from a fortress, ships or artillery at a sector or a ship.
  - Air Mission: fly or drop cargo, paradrop, bomb (pinpoint or
    strategic) and recon.  Click an airfield to pick its planes; no
    escorts is fine.
  - Distribute and Threshold, showing the sector's current settings.
  - Right-click: Distribute and Threshold on your sectors; Attack and
    Fire on others; Fly or Bomb on sectors with your planes.
  Fixes:
  - Right-click menu items did nothing: the menu was destroyed before
    the chosen item could run.

GtkACE 0.5.0 (2026-11-07)

  Telegram window (Diplomacy -> Telegrams, Ctrl+T, the toolbar's
  Telegrams button, or click the mail notice in the status bar):
  - Telegrams, bulletins, production reports and announcements are
    captured whenever "read" or "wire" runs and kept in the game
    database, so they stay after the server deletes them.  Duplicates
    are skipped.
  - Folders: all received, telegrams, bulletins, production reports,
    announcements and sent, with unread counts.  Unread messages are in
    bold; the window opens at the oldest unread one.
  - Check for New, New, Reply (quoting the original), Forward, Delete,
    Previous and Next.
  - Writing: choose a country or "Everyone" for an announcement.  Lines
    are sent in answer to the server's prompts; blank lines, "." and
    "~x" lines are protected so they don't end or abort the telegram.
    Shows the length against the server's 1024-character limit and keeps
    a copy in Sent.
  - Option to delete telegrams from the server once GtkACE has them.
  - AutoRead now stores arriving telegrams in the window.
  - The status bar shows the number of unread messages.

GtkACE 0.4.0 (2026-11-07)

  Command dialogs (Commands menu, and the map's right-click menu):
  - Move (Ctrl+M): commodity, amount, from and to.  Click the map to
    pick the sectors.  GtkACE asks the server for the best path and the
    exact mobility cost ("bestpath" and "test"), shows how much mobility
    will be left, and draws the path on the map.  Test and Move buttons.
  - Navigate ships (Ctrl+N) and march land units: click a sector with
    your units to pick them, then click the destination, or type a
    route.  The server finds the way; GtkACE stops the units there.
  - Build (Ctrl+B): ships, land units, planes, nukes, bridge spans and
    bridge towers.  The type list shows each type's materials, work and
    cost from the server, and which need more tech than you have.  The
    kind is chosen from the sector (harbor, headquarters, airfield ...).
  - Load or unload ships (Ctrl+L) and land units: commodities, planes
    or land units, showing what the carrier has aboard and what the
    sector has.
  - Each dialog shows the exact command it will send.
  - Right-click a sector: Move From Here, Build Here, and for sectors
    with your ships or land units, Navigate/March and Load/Unload.

GtkACE 0.3.0 (2026-11-07)

  Intelligence on other countries:
  - Output of your commands is read for sightings, as WinACE does:
    lookout, llook, coastwatch, skywatch, sonar and spy reports (and
    anything else printing the same lines).  Sectors and units seen are
    kept in the game database with the time and the command that saw
    them.
  - Other countries' sectors are drawn in their player colours.  Their
    ships, land units and planes use WinACE's icons: red for countries
    you are at war with or hostile to, green for friendly or allied,
    blue for neutral, and grey for sightings more than a day old.
  - The sector panel shows what was seen of a foreign sector (owner,
    efficiency, people, stocks, roads, defence) and when, and lists
    foreign units seen there.
  - Units window has a Foreign tab (Ctrl+5) listing every sighting.
  - Reports -> Intelligence menu: lookout, land lookout, radar, land
    radar, sonar, coastwatch, skywatch, spy.
  - File -> Clear Intelligence forgets all sightings.
  - Relations are read from the server, and re-read after declare.
  Fixes:
  - Server tables with array fields (such as relations) are now stored
    correctly: one column per element.

GtkACE 0.2.0 (2026-11-07)

  Units:
  - Ships, land units, planes and nukes are read from the server (xdump)
    and drawn on the map with WinACE's unit icons; View menu switches
    each kind on or off.
  - New Units window (Units menu, Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+4): sortable lists of
    ships, land units, planes and nukes with location, efficiency,
    mobility, tech, cargo, fleet/army/wing and what each is loaded on.
    Double-click a unit to find it on the map.
  - The sector panel lists the units in the selected sector.
  - Right-click menu lists the ships, land units or planes in a sector.
  - Units menu also runs cargo, lcargo, sstat, lstat, pstat and show build.
  - Refresh -> Update Units.
  Other:
  - After commands that change sectors or units (move, navigate, build,
    designate, load, fly ...), GtkACE quietly re-reads sectors, units and
    the bmap so the map stays current.
  - Table descriptions are fetched once per login, so refreshes send
    less traffic.

GtkACE 0.1.0 (2026-11-07)

  First release: a port of WinACE 2.5.72 to C and GTK 3.
  - Game list and login dialog; async connect and Empire login.
  - Command line with history, server questions, Escape to abort.
  - Telegram/announcement notices and AutoRead.
  - SQLite database built from xdump; bmap parsing.
  - Hex map with sector details panel and right-click commands.
  - Offline mode; report menus and toolbar.
  Tested against Wolfpack Empire 4.4.0.
